      "description": "The meme promotes a misogynistic message by implying that male athletes inherently dominate sports traditionally associated with women, suggesting their victory is due to gender rather than skill. This reinforces the harmful stereotype that women are less capable in sports, thereby devaluing female athletes and their achievements.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cc21361e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0953d281",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience for this meme is individuals who hold or are exposed to misogynistic and sexist worldviews, particularly those who believe in gender-based sporting advantage and who may devalue female athletes by attributing male success to inherent gender superiority rather than skill or merit. The meme is designed to resonate with communities that reinforce harmful gender stereotypes, such as those who view sports as inherently male-dominated and who may mock or dismiss the legitimacy of women's sports. The visual of boys playing soccer and the text 'he won because he is a boy' are crafted to appeal to audiences who find humor or validation in the idea that men are naturally superior in sports, thereby promoting a toxic and misogynistic message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cc21361e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
